# React Flow render

Follow `packages/app/REACTFLOW_RENDER.md`. The App renders **execution manifests (v2)** with the
graph model: nodes, branches, ports, containers — see `realignment/graph-model.md`.

Non-negotiables:

- Published edges are **data** only. Layout `control` edges are stripped before publish.
- **`if`**, **`parallel`**, **`loop`**, and loop **`end`** (`end:<loopId>`) are React Flow nodes with typed ports.
- Branches are drawn only for **`$ref`** bindings; resolve producers per C1 (inputs, `as`, loop item/index,
  if/parallel scoped `as`, loop `into` from `end` `results`).
- Data branches only (`$ref` / `$state`); structure nodes (`if` / `parallel` / `loop` / `end`) with ports; no legacy sequence-connector UI.
- Frames (`ecp-frame`) outline containers with bands; start / `end` nodes pin to the left / right
  stroke. Band clusters are dagre parents; frames are not `parentId` in React Flow.